{
 "_": "The patches for the battle jacket in a person's Profile on the CB. Ryan's brief, 2026-10-14. Written into patches.js, the rooms and lib.mjs by tools/make-patches.py; see its docstring for what it refuses.",
 "_draw": "Every patch is drawn from `draw` and nothing else: [\"path\", d, fill, stroke, width] and [\"text\", x, y, size, face, fill, words, length], in millimetres inside a w by h patch. A colour is a custom property love.css declares in :root, or a hex. Each patch is drawn in its own room's inks and faces, as a souvenir of that room, and on the jacket they are all together, which is what a battle jacket is. `length` is the text's textLength, so the words fit the patch whatever font the browser ends up with.",
 "_how": "`scattered` is lying somewhere in its room and is picked up; `shop` is on a counter or a table in a shop and is taken. Neither has a price: nothing on this street is for sale but what is in the honesty box.",
